    success: 'the student solves at least 7 of 10 puzzles and can read an if / else program aloud correctly.',
    misconceptions: ['Thinking the else part also runs when the condition is true.', 'Putting the if / else outside the loop, so it only checks once.', 'Checking path ahead before tank ahead (a tank blocks the path).'],
    support: 'provide the loop and if / else shell; students choose the condition and actions. Lesson 12 offers easier practice.', extension: '3 stars on 11.5, 11.8 and 11.10; design a maze that needs a nested if / else.',
